        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "122f80fb-0d86-53cc-b3ba-8f24939afe6f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Horton Foote, David Foster Wallace, Thomas C. Ryan, K.B. Gilden, Katya Gilden, Bert Gilden\n- Works: To Kill a Mockingbird, Tender Mercies, Hurry Sundown, Hurry Sundown novel\n- Topics: American writing, screenwriting, playwriting, television drama, pseudonyms\n\nFacts:\n- Horton Foote was an American playwright and screenwriter born on March 14, 1916, and he died on March 4, 2009.\n- Horton Foote was known for the screenplays for the 1962 film To Kill a Mockingbird and the 1983 film Tender Mercies, as well as for live television dramas during the Golden Age of Television.\n- David Foster Wallace was an American writer and university instructor of English and creative writing who was born on February 21, 1962, and died on September 12, 2008.\n- The 1965 novel Hurry Sundown was credited to K.B. Gilden, which was a pseudonym used by the married couple Katya Gilden and Bert Gilden.\n- The screenplay for the film Hurry Sundown was written by Horton Foote and Thomas C. Ryan and was based on the 1965 novel of the same title.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
